  "learningBlocks": [
    {
      "id": "l7-b1",
      "type": "concept",
      "title": "Who does the action?",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Active voice presents the subject as performing the action. Passive voice presents the subject as receiving it. Lesson 7 adds that contrast without adding a large new vocabulary burden.",
        "fr": "À l'actif, le sujet accomplit l'action ; au passif, il la reçoit. La leçon 7 ajoute ce contraste sans alourdir fortement le vocabulaire."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l7-b2",
      "type": "morphology",
      "title": "Read passive endings as signals",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "High-yield present passive endings include -r, -ris, -tur, -mur, -mini and -ntur. First learn to recognize them in context; full production can come later.",
        "fr": "Les terminaisons passives importantes comprennent -r, -ris, -tur, -mur, -mini et -ntur. Il faut d'abord les reconnaître en contexte ; la production complète viendra ensuite."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l7-b3",
      "type": "authentic-example",
      "title": "sanctificetur",
      "sourceId": "mr1962-pater-sanctificetur-l7",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "sanctificetur contains the passive signal -tur: the name receives the action of sanctifying. Its subjunctive mood is deliberately deferred; the reading target here is voice.",
        "fr": "sanctificetur contient le signal passif -tur : le nom reçoit l'action de sanctifier. Le subjonctif est volontairement reporté ; ici, la cible est la voix."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "mr1962-pater-sanctificetur-l7",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l7-b4",
      "type": "contrast",
      "title": "Laudamus versus sanctificetur",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Laudamus means that 'we' perform the praising; sanctificetur means that the subject is to be sanctified. Read the direction of the action before translating mechanically.",
        "fr": "Laudamus signifie que « nous » accomplissons l'action de louer ; sanctificetur signifie que le sujet reçoit l'action de sanctifier. Lisez d'abord le sens de l'action."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l7-b5",
      "type": "boundary",
      "title": "Not every passive-looking form is a finite passive",
      "sourceId": "mr1962-sanctus-benedictus-l7",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Benedictus is passive in origin but functions here as a participial adjective, 'blessed'. Context prevents a false rule that every -tus form is a present passive verb.",
        "fr": "Benedictus est d'origine passive mais fonctionne ici comme adjectif participial, « béni ». Le contexte empêche de croire que toute forme en -tus est un verbe passif au présent."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "mr1962-sanctus-benedictus-l7",
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l7-b6",
      "type": "retrieval",
      "title": "Grammar grows while vocabulary stays controlled",
      "learnerCopy": {
        "en": "Only sanctifico is new tracked vocabulary. The real work is to reread known verbs and nouns through the active/passive distinction while keeping the permanent case map alive.",
        "fr": "Seul sanctifico est nouveau dans le vocabulaire suivi. Le vrai travail consiste à relire les verbes et noms déjà connus à travers l'opposition actif/passif tout en conservant la carte des cas."
      },
      "referenceIds": [
        "grammar-scanlon-1944",
        "grammar-petitmangin-1930",
        "curriculum-latin-course-40-v1"
      ]
    }
  ],
